# iotgw local file contexts.
#
# Everything on /data that file_contexts.subs does not alias onto another path
# (OTA state, the encrypted-store image, overlay work directories, iotgw state)
# is persistent service state: var_lib_t, as under /var/lib.
#
# Typed exceptions live HERE and not in the iotgw policy module's .fc on
# purpose: a file_contexts.local entry takes precedence over any module .fc
# entry for the same path (semanage-fcontext(8)), so a module .fc line for a
# /data path would silently lose to the var_lib_t default below. Keeping every
# typed /data path in this one file leaves a single precedence domain, where
# the more specific spec wins. Verify on target with matchpathcon; the build
# does not check the precedence.
/data(/.*)?	system_u:object_r:var_lib_t:s0

# Private half of the OTA identity (crypt-bundle decryption key, streaming TLS
# key). Readers: rauc_t and the unconfined domains; see policy/iotgw.te.
/data/ota/certs/device\.key	--	system_u:object_r:iotgw_ota_key_t:s0

# RAUC runtime state under data-directory=/data/.
/data/central\.raucs	--	system_u:object_r:rauc_var_lib_t:s0
/data/rauc-events\.log.*	--	system_u:object_r:rauc_var_lib_t:s0

# Local bundle staging for `rauc install <file>` (an OTA download streams over
# HTTPS and needs no file). RAUC's own type, so rauc_t reads a staged bundle
# without a grant on the var_lib_t default that covers every other service's
# state under /data.
/data/ota/bundles(/.*)?	system_u:object_r:rauc_var_lib_t:s0
# Bundle staging for `rauc install <file>`: the operator writes here, rauc_t reads.
/data/ota-tmp(/.*)?	system_u:object_r:iotgw_ota_inbox_t:s0

# Broker persistence and edge-healthd state.
/data/mosquitto(/.*)?	system_u:object_r:iotgw_mosquitto_var_lib_t:s0
/data/edge/health(/.*)?	system_u:object_r:iotgw_healthd_var_lib_t:s0
